==> Caveats
==> opencv@4
opencv@4 is keg-only, which means it was not symlinked into /opt/homebrew,
because this is an alternate version of another formula.

If you need to have opencv@4 first in your PATH, run:
  echo 'export PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/opencv@4/bin:$PATH' >> ~/.zshrc

For compilers to find opencv@4 you may need to set:
  export LDFLAGS=-L/opt/homebrew/opt/opencv@4/lib
  export CPPFLAGS=-I/opt/homebrew/opt/opencv@4/include

For pkgconf to find opencv@4 you may need to set:
  export PKG_CONFIG_PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/opencv@4/lib/pkgconfig

For cmake to find opencv@4 you may need to set:
  export CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/opencv@4

The following opencv@4 executables are shadowed by other linked Homebrew commands:
  opencv_annotation (shadowed by /opt/homebrew/bin/opencv_annotation from opencv)
  opencv_model_diagnostics (shadowed by /opt/homebrew/bin/opencv_model_diagnostics from opencv)
  opencv_version (shadowed by /opt/homebrew/bin/opencv_version from opencv)
  opencv_visualisation (shadowed by /opt/homebrew/bin/opencv_visualisation from opencv)
  opencv_waldboost_detector (shadowed by /opt/homebrew/bin/opencv_waldboost_detector from opencv)
Running these by name will not invoke the version provided by this formula.
Run `brew link opencv@4` to switch the active version to this keg.
Disable this behaviour by setting `HOMEBREW_NO_PATH_SHADOW_CHECK=1`.
Hide these hints with `HOMEBREW_NO_ENV_HINTS=1` (see `man brew`).
